Z||000000||Chance||06-02-2000||04:30 AM||||Which one of these have you guys tried, and what do you reccomend. I was looking at the Fiero Store, and I seen the E-tron control module, and the Acell one for about 25USD more.  and then the E-tron coil, or the Acell SUPER coil for 35USD more?<BR>Chance||||reg||1
Z||000001||lennyb4||06-02-2000||09:03 AM||||You can get the e-tron at any major automotive parts store (forest shity, murrys, etc..) but to be honest i would go with the Acell parts. Also check this place out im sure their cheaper then the fiero store for the same parts and they can ship either overnight or nextday to most areas.. <A HREF="http://www.summitracing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.summitracing.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by lennyb4 (edited 06-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||06-02-2000||09:22 AM||||At least for a V6 control module I would only buy GM AC-Delco OEM. I have tried non OEM and they fry in less than 15K mi. I think maybe the ACCEL could be trusted but if it cost more than the OEM I would go OEM.||||reg||1
